WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.353
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.080
Micro air vehicles present
a very appealing platform

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:17.980
for search and rescue, civil
engineering inspection,

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.600
and a myriad of
other tasks where

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.600
it would be difficult or
dangerous to send a human.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.590
By flying over
difficult terrain,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:27.490
MAVs skip many of the
most challenging aspects

00:00:27.490 --> 00:00:30.640
of using a ground vehicle
to carry out these missions.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.070
In environments where
GPS is available,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:34.960
many researchers have
developed systems

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:37.690
capable of high-level
autonomous behaviors.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.030
The Robust Robotics Group
and the Computer Science

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:43.180
and Artificial Intelligence
Laboratory at MIT

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.280
has developed a micro
air vehicle capable

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.470
of high-level
autonomous behaviors

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.350
in unconstrained
GPS-denied environments.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.230
We have outfitted a quad
rotor helicopter developed

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:56.170
in collaboration with
Ascending Technologies

00:00:56.170 --> 00:00:58.210
with a suite of
sensors and algorithms

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.160
that successfully
closed the loop

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.580
and stabilize the vehicle
in unknown environments.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.950
Using a lightweight
laser scanner,

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:08.890
we're able to perform
high-resolution scan matching

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.240
in real time to estimate the
vehicle's relative position.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:15.550
These state estimates
are accurate enough

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.860
that we can accurately
identify and locate

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.490
a window in a 3D point cloud
generated from the raw laser

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:22.990
scans.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.260
This narrow window not
much wider than a vehicle

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.390
highlights the accuracy
and performance

00:01:28.390 --> 00:01:31.780
of our state estimation
and control algorithms.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.000
The laser and
stereo camera allows

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.720
us to perform obstacle
avoidance in 3D.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:41.590
The real-time state sensing
and state estimation algorithms

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:44.890
provide us with a very
stable and robust platform

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:47.740
on which to build a suite of
high-level mapping and planning

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:50.920
capabilities that do not
need to take into account

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:54.850
the fast and unstable
micro air vehicle dynamics.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:56.410
We have integrated
the quad rotor

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:01.030
with a SLAM solution that allows
us to map unknown environments.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.190
The map generated by
the SLAM algorithm

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.860
also allows us to perform
completely autonomous

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:09.070
exploration of
unknown environments.

00:02:09.070 --> 00:02:11.320
The exploration module
seeks to balance

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.290
learning the geometrical
extent of the environment

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:18.370
with sweeping known boundaries
of the map for a visual target.

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:20.710
This process must also
choose trajectories

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:24.190
that ensure the vehicle
remains well localized.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.650
This research culminated
in our team's entry

00:02:26.650 --> 00:02:30.610
into the 2009 AUVSI
International Aerial Robotics

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:31.990
Competition.

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:34.990
The mission was executed
completely autonomously.

00:02:34.990 --> 00:02:37.540
The vehicle had to
take off, detect,

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.690
and fly through a window,
explore an unknown environment

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:44.380
to find a designated control
panel using the onboard color

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.765
camera.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.140
Our vehicle completed the
fifth mission in the first year

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:48.940
it was held--

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:51.580
a feat that had not been
achieved in the 19-year history

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:54.660
of the IARC competitions.

